cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "SportsBioMechanicsAnalyzer (SBMA)"
abstract: >-
  A freely available Windows desktop application for marker-less two- and
  three-dimensional sports motion analysis from ordinary video. It integrates
  multi-camera synchronisation, camera calibration (2D/3D DLT, the 3D CC method
  using feature points on the field, and ChArUco stereo calibration),
  deep-learning pose estimation (RF-DETR and RTMPose, 23 body points) with
  manual correction, Butterworth smoothing with automatic cut-off selection
  (Winter's residual analysis), multi-camera triangulation, kinematic graphs
  and sport-specific analysis templates into a single workflow. It also imports
  C3D files with force plates and calculates joint moments by inverse dynamics.
type: software
